Comment: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{=50}===============================DIALOGUE============================
Dialogue: 50,0:01:54.98,0:01:58.36,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\an8}[USOPP]\NI can't believe our luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.40,0:01:59.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Seriously.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:59.49,0:02:01.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\an8}That orangutan almost sunk us.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:01.87,0:02:05.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\an8}And now it's up to me to fix it\Nall and keep this thing afloat.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:05.20,0:02:06.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[ZORO]\NSeems to me\Nthat this busted old ship
Dialogue: 50,0:02:06.87,0:02:08.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,is on her last leg.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:08.21,0:02:09.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We need a new one.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:09.21,0:02:11.71,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,How dare you even consider\Nreplacing this boat?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:11.75,0:02:12.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah, how dare you!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:12.70,0:02:14.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We all know the story, Usopp.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:14.57,0:02:16.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And try not to be so defensive.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:16.91,0:02:19.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The Going Merry is an\Nimportant part of our crew,
Dialogue: 50,0:02:19.12,0:02:21.46,Secondary-207-,,0,0,0,,{\an8}and we all know we have\Nto take care of her.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:21.50,0:02:23.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't take\Neverything so personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.67,0:02:25.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're right. I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:27.92,0:02:28.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NOops!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.92,0:02:30.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[screams]
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.59,0:02:31.55,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:32.09,0:02:33.93,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NWe left Mock Town\Nand headed east
Dialogue: 50,0:02:33.97,0:02:36.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,by circling around the\Nnorthern shore of the island.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:36.60,0:02:38.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Our destination is here.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:38.73,0:02:40.23,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We're supposed\Nto meet that man there.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:40.27,0:02:40.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What's his name?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:40.98,0:02:42.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,His name is Mont Blanc Cricket.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.90,0:02:43.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NAnd you're sure that
Dialogue: 50,0:02:43.77,0:02:46.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,he'll be able to\Nhelp us out, right?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:46.68,0:02:48.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Whoa! Amazing!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:49.93,0:02:51.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NThat's where he lives?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:51.41,0:02:52.94,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's a freakin' palace!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:52.94,0:02:55.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[USOPP]\NI've never seen\Na house that big before.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:55.31,0:02:57.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This Mont Blanc Cricket\Nguy must be really loaded.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.02,0:02:59.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Ugh. Look closer.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:59.82,0:03:01.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's really unattractive.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:01.71,0:03:04.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A guy's gotta have some serious\Nguts to build a house that ugly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.95,0:03:07.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hmm? What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.41,0:03:11.71,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[screams]
Dialogue: 50,0:03:11.75,0:03:13.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This isn't a palace at all!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:13.67,0:03:14.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}[CHOPPER, USOPP]\N– What?\N– What?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:14.67,0:03:16.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[ZORO]\NThe actual house\Nis only half that size.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:16.80,0:03:17.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What you see is a facade.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.97,0:03:19.01,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A fake.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:19.07,0:03:20.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SANJI]\NThis guy's even\Nmore vain than I thought.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:20.87,0:03:23.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why exactly did Cricket\Ndecide to leave his home
Dialogue: 50,0:03:23.41,0:03:24.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and come live here?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:24.87,0:03:26.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[ROBIN]\NI don't know all the details.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:26.71,0:03:28.96,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But I think it has something\Nto do with his belief
Dialogue: 50,0:03:29.00,0:03:30.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,that a large amount\Nof gold rests somewhere
Dialogue: 50,0:03:30.80,0:03:31.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,in the hills of Jaya.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:31.92,0:03:32.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,G‐Gold?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:32.63,0:03:33.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you think he's here searching
Dialogue: 50,0:03:33.80,0:03:35.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,for some sort of\Nburied treasure?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:35.55,0:03:37.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Well, I just don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.14,0:03:40.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NGold!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:40.10,0:03:41.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Try over here, Chopper.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:41.49,0:03:42.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Dig up this spot.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:42.57,0:03:44.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NI'll be right there, Nami.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:44.45,0:03:46.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SANJI]\NIt must be hard to live\Nalone in such a remote area.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:46.90,0:03:48.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NHello!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:48.11,0:03:49.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't just barge in there.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:49.95,0:03:51.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Huh. Looks like nobody's home.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.03,0:03:54.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Anybody here?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:54.52,0:03:55.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I guess he's gone.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:55.70,0:03:56.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Get out of there, you idiot.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:56.70,0:03:58.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This guy could be dangerous.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:58.77,0:03:59.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NHey, you guys.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:59.92,0:04:01.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Nobody's home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.09,0:04:04.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Huh... What's this?
Dialogue: 50,0:04:05.57,0:04:07.11,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A book.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:07.18,0:04:09.31,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And it looks pretty old.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:09.98,0:04:12.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's called "Noland, the Liar."
Dialogue: 50,0:04:12.66,0:04:14.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Huh. Sounds like\Nit could be good.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:14.96,0:04:16.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I sure like the title.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:16.87,0:04:18.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SANJI]\N"Noland, the Liar"?
Dialogue: 50,0:04:18.50,0:04:19.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah, have you heard of it?
Dialogue: 50,0:04:19.75,0:04:20.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It says here,
Dialogue: 50,0:04:20.96,0:04:23.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,it was originally published\Nin the North Blue territory.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:23.34,0:04:24.25,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It was!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:24.35,0:04:25.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I was born in the\NNorth Blue territory.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:26.01,0:04:28.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm certain I must\Nhave told you guys that.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:28.39,0:04:29.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,No, that's news to me.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:29.73,0:04:31.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I always thought that\Nyou were born in the East.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:31.56,0:04:32.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SANJI]\NI grew up there.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:32.52,0:04:33.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Enough already, Chopper.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:33.57,0:04:34.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.71,0:04:36.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[screams]
Dialogue: 50,0:04:36.74,0:04:39.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Where I come from,\Nthis is a famous story.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:39.25,0:04:42.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,1918)}It's a fairy tale supposedly\Nbased on the life of Noland,
Dialogue: 50,0:04:42.50,0:04:45.51,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,1918)}who lived in the\NNorth Blue a long time ago.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:48.13,0:04:51.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NThis is a story\Nof ancient origins.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:51.10,0:04:55.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The events herein transpired\Nmore than 400 years ago.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:55.85,0:04:59.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,There once was a man by\Nthe name of Mont Blanc Noland
Dialogue: 50,0:04:59.09,0:05:01.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who lived in the\NNorth Blue countryside.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:01.97,0:05:05.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland, who was an explorer,\Nalways regaled the crowds
Dialogue: 50,0:05:05.78,0:05:08.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,with stories of his\Nincredible exploits.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:08.10,0:05:09.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But nobody knew whether or not
Dialogue: 50,0:05:09.22,0:05:12.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to take Noland's\Ntall tales seriously.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:12.63,0:05:15.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,One day, upon returning\Nfrom yet another adventure,
Dialogue: 50,0:05:15.85,0:05:18.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,he reported to his king\Nall that he had seen.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:18.73,0:05:21.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,"I saw a city of gold on\Nan island in the great sea,"
Dialogue: 50,0:05:21.73,0:05:22.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,declared Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:22.90,0:05:24.23,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And the courageous king decided
Dialogue: 50,0:05:24.28,0:05:28.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\pos(720,1053)}that he must have this\Ntreasure for his kingdom.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:28.29,0:05:30.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The king set out with Noland\Nand two thousand
Dialogue: 50,0:05:30.53,0:05:31.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,of his finest soldiers.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:31.99,0:05:34.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Along the way they\Nendured treacherous storms
Dialogue: 50,0:05:34.32,0:05:37.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and battled many\Nferocious sea creatures.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:37.16,0:05:40.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,At the end of their journey\Nonly the King, Noland,
Dialogue: 50,0:05:40.16,0:05:42.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and 100 soldiers\Nsurvived to set foot
Dialogue: 50,0:05:42.53,0:05:44.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,on the island that\Nhoused the city of gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.06,0:05:46.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And all they found\Nfor their troubles
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.18,0:05:50.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,was a normal island covered\Nwith an ordinary jungle.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:50.15,0:05:53.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And so, upon their return,\NNoland was sentenced to death
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.69,0:05:55.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,for the crime of\Nlying to his King.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:55.77,0:05:58.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,His last words were as follows.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:58.69,0:06:02.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,"I can only assume that the\Ncity of gold sunk into the sea."
Dialogue: 50,0:06:02.32,0:06:04.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The King and his\Ncourt were dumbfounded.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:04.28,0:06:06.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Nobody believed Noland anymore.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:06.37,0:06:09.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And the last of his days were\Nspent in shame and ridicule
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.33,0:06:11.25,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,before his sentence\Nof death was carried out
Dialogue: 50,0:06:11.29,0:06:13.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,before a cheering crowd.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:13.71,0:06:14.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It says here that\Nthe book is based
Dialogue: 50,0:06:14.92,0:06:17.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,on the true story\Nof Noland, the Liar.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:17.89,0:06:20.19,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[BELLAMY laughs]
Dialogue: 50,0:06:20.30,0:06:22.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Mont Blanc Cricket\Nis a descendant
Dialogue: 50,0:06:22.13,0:06:25.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,of the infamous\NMontblanc Noland?
Dialogue: 50,0:06:26.01,0:06:28.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I heard that fairy tale\Nall the time as a kid.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:28.26,0:06:29.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But I never knew that\NJaya was the island
Dialogue: 50,0:06:29.90,0:06:31.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,where he thought\Nhe saw the city of gold.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:31.99,0:06:33.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,When we were growing up\Nin the North Blue,
Dialogue: 50,0:06:33.82,0:06:34.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,we were always warned
Dialogue: 50,0:06:34.91,0:06:37.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,that if we lied, we'd suffer\Nthe same fate as Noland
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.61,0:06:40.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and be ridiculed until we\Nwere eventually put to death.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:40.20,0:06:41.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 50,0:06:41.95,0:06:45.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It makes sense that\NCricket's related to that fool,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.08,0:06:48.55,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,but I can't believe that Jaya is\Nthe island from the fairy tale.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:48.83,0:06:51.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Pardon the intrusion,\Nbut if I heard you correctly,
Dialogue: 50,0:06:51.12,0:06:53.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,you're saying a descendant\Nof Noland is here,
Dialogue: 50,0:06:53.13,0:06:55.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,400 years after the fact,\Nlooking for that gold?
Dialogue: 50,0:06:55.97,0:06:58.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,He's gotta be doing this\Nto clear his family name
Dialogue: 50,0:06:58.26,0:07:00.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and regain some\Nsmall amount of respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.97,0:07:05.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 50,0:07:05.86,0:07:07.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This story keeps getting\Nbetter and better.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.13,0:07:09.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 50,0:07:09.88,0:07:11.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Can he seriously\Nhope to wipe away
Dialogue: 50,0:07:11.84,0:07:13.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,over 400 years\Nof embarrassment
Dialogue: 50,0:07:13.17,0:07:15.38,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,by bringing back\Na few pieces of gold?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.42,0:07:16.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What a joke!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:18.01,0:07:21.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Sounds like he's a\Nfew bricks short of a wall.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:29.98,0:07:31.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NAlas, the Liar died
Dialogue: 50,0:07:31.97,0:07:34.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,before he could prove\Nhimself to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.94,0:07:35.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 50,0:07:36.02,0:07:37.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All he ever really wanted to do
Dialogue: 50,0:07:37.81,0:07:40.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,was live the life\Nof an adventurer.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:40.73,0:07:41.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[USOPP]\NThat last part's\Nnot in the book.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:41.90,0:07:44.36,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't try to tack on your\Nown sentimental nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.40,0:07:46.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY screams]
Dialogue: 50,0:07:46.03,0:07:48.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Did he just fall in the water?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:48.20,0:07:49.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:50.58,0:07:52.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NWho the hell are you?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:52.12,0:07:53.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You've got nerve,
Dialogue: 50,0:07:53.16,0:07:55.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,relaxing at someone's\Nhouse without permission.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:55.66,0:07:57.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This is my land,\Nand I suggest you leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.88,0:08:00.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hurry, Usopp. Move it! Go and\Nfish Luffy out of the sea.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:00.50,0:08:01.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know why you're here.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:01.76,0:08:03.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're after my gold!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.02,0:08:12.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Sanji!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.01,0:08:14.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Sanji, no!
Dialogue: 50,0:08:14.84,0:08:17.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.\NThis guy's a terrible shot.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:19.02,0:08:20.11,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SANJI]\NHey! Cut it out!
Dialogue: 50,0:08:20.15,0:08:20.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Idiot.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:20.85,0:08:22.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Never underestimate your foe.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.15,0:08:26.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[ZORO]\NOut of the way.\NI'll handle this.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:34.57,0:08:36.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You really need to\Nlearn to be more careful.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:36.20,0:08:38.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But I thought I saw...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.22,0:08:40.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,...bubbles in the water,
Dialogue: 50,0:08:40.47,0:08:43.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,so I looked closer and\Nthen a chestnut appeared.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:43.14,0:08:44.39,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But it wasn't a chestnut.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.43,0:08:48.01,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It was a guy,\Nand he pulled me in.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:49.31,0:08:50.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NWhat's with him?
Dialogue: 50,0:08:52.48,0:08:54.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NI need more cold towels.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:54.36,0:08:56.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And open up those windows.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:57.16,0:08:58.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[ZORO]\NWhat's Caisson disease?
Dialogue: 50,0:08:58.82,0:09:00.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NSo this guy is really sick, huh?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:00.37,0:09:01.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:01.62,0:09:04.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Caisson disease is an illness\Nthat sometimes afflicts divers.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:04.35,0:09:05.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Though it's called a disease,
Dialogue: 50,0:09:05.22,0:09:07.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,it isn't actually\Na chronic condition.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:07.56,0:09:09.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's caused by a lack\Nof decompression
Dialogue: 50,0:09:09.44,0:09:11.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,when surfacing from the seabed.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:11.40,0:09:13.82,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The nitrogen in the\Nblood releases too quickly
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.86,0:09:17.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and causes gas bubbles to\Nform in the circulatory system.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:17.77,0:09:18.94,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And when those\Ngas bubbles expand
Dialogue: 50,0:09:18.97,0:09:21.94,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,they can cause considerable\Ndamage to muscles and joints
Dialogue: 50,0:09:21.94,0:09:24.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and seriously\Ndecrease blood flow.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:24.10,0:09:25.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So it's a mystery disease.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:25.72,0:09:26.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Think you can help him?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:26.86,0:09:28.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NI'm not sure.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:28.07,0:09:30.36,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,My guess is he kept diving\Neveryday without allowing time
Dialogue: 50,0:09:30.40,0:09:33.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,for his body to recover and\Nit finally caught up with him.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:33.64,0:09:35.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That's why he passed\Nout during the fight.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:35.31,0:09:37.39,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But why in the world\Ndid he do that?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:37.68,0:09:38.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NI don't know,
Dialogue: 50,0:09:38.72,0:09:40.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,but he was taking a big risk.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:40.90,0:09:43.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,In some cases,\NCaisson disease can cause death.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:43.99,0:09:46.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So he's lucky to be alive.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:58.46,0:09:59.71,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SHOJO]\NOh hey, Masira.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:59.76,0:10:01.34,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I guess you're\Nstill alive after all.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:01.35,0:10:02.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[MASIRA]\NWhy do you say that?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:03.01,0:10:04.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SHOJO]\NForget about it.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:04.15,0:10:06.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you know what all that\Ngunfire was about earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.15,0:10:07.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[MASIRA]\NI'm not sure,
Dialogue: 50,0:10:07.11,0:10:09.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,but that's where I'm\Nheaded now, to find out.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:09.40,0:10:10.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SHOJO]\NWell, come on then.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:10.36,0:10:12.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm worried about the old‐timer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.26,0:10:17.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey, Old‐timer.\NAre you all right?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:17.31,0:10:20.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[screams]\NThey've come to kill us.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:20.60,0:10:22.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What in the world are\Nyou people doing here?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:22.97,0:10:24.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And just what are\Nyou doing to our friend?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:25.02,0:10:25.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We're trying to help.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:25.94,0:10:27.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So I suggest you\Neither lend us a hand
Dialogue: 50,0:10:27.90,0:10:29.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,or find someone else to bother.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:29.32,0:10:30.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't antagonize them, Luffy.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:30.49,0:10:31.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You know what\Nthey're capable of,
Dialogue: 50,0:10:31.56,0:10:33.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and now there're two of\Nthose savages to deal with.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:33.98,0:10:35.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NThey're savages!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:35.14,0:10:38.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[USOPP]\NEveryone, jump out\Nthe windows and run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.15,0:10:40.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Thank you, guys.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:40.94,0:10:41.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[USOPP]\NWhat did they say?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:42.82,0:10:44.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NSo you guys\Nlive on this island, too?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:45.16,0:10:47.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yep. This old‐timer's house\Nis the official headquarters
Dialogue: 50,0:10:47.99,0:10:50.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,of the Saruyama\NAlliance of Jaya.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:50.16,0:10:51.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We call this home,
Dialogue: 50,0:10:51.12,0:10:53.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,but we spend most of\Nour time on our ships.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:53.17,0:10:54.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We're more comfortable at sea
Dialogue: 50,0:10:54.06,0:10:56.02,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,'cause this place\Nis too small for us.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:56.02,0:10:58.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NYou guys are\Ntoo big for your own good.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:58.52,0:11:00.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But it's all in how\Nyou look at it, I guess.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:00.11,0:11:01.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,To a giant you'd still look like
Dialogue: 50,0:11:01.46,0:11:02.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,nothing more\Nthan a ball of earwax.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.95,0:11:03.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[laughter]
Dialogue: 50,0:11:03.91,0:11:05.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Well, those three sure\Nare getting along well,
Dialogue: 50,0:11:05.84,0:11:06.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,now, aren't they?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:06.84,0:11:08.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah, seems like they\Nhave a lot in common.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:08.89,0:11:09.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm pretty impressed you managed
Dialogue: 50,0:11:09.70,0:11:10.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to get Masira\Nhere off your ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.96,0:11:14.42,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's quite a feat for someone as\Nsmall as you to overpower him.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:14.46,0:11:15.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NEh, it wasn't really that hard.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:15.92,0:11:17.04,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's that?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:17.08,0:11:19.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NI'm sure you could kick his ass.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:19.63,0:11:21.42,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Luffy! He's waking up!
Dialogue: 50,0:11:21.46,0:11:22.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,He's awake?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:25.92,0:11:26.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[SHOJO]\NHe's right!
Dialogue: 50,0:11:26.76,0:11:29.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I can kick Masira's ass!
Dialogue: 50,0:11:30.68,0:11:31.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NHey, chestnut head.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:31.76,0:11:34.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I got a question for ya.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.85,0:11:37.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 50,0:11:37.77,0:11:39.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I attacked you.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:39.57,0:11:41.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I thought you were nothing more\Nthan another group of bandits
Dialogue: 50,0:11:41.78,0:11:43.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who had come to steal my gold.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:43.49,0:11:45.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Did someone say\Nsomething about gold?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:45.50,0:11:46.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Just calm down, Nami.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:46.50,0:11:48.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What exactly was it\Nyou wanted to ask me?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:48.92,0:11:51.71,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We're searching for sky island\Nand were told you might be able
Dialogue: 50,0:11:51.75,0:11:53.36,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to tell us how to get there.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:53.36,0:11:55.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NAre you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.54,0:11:58.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 50,0:11:58.81,0:12:01.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you really\Nbelieve that place exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.71,0:12:03.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey! Stop it.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:03.41,0:12:04.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You can't attack a sick man.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:04.67,0:12:06.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You mean there's no sky island?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.50,0:12:07.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.63,0:12:12.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I don't know. See...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.92,0:12:16.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Nobody knows if the\Nsky island really exists or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.68,0:12:17.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know of only one man
Dialogue: 50,0:12:17.68,0:12:20.31,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who claims to have seen\Nthe island for himself.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:20.32,0:12:23.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But he's considered\Na liar of epic proportions.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.61,0:12:24.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wah!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:24.20,0:12:26.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What are you looking at?
Dialogue: 50,0:12:26.62,0:12:27.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NThere's an old fairy tale
Dialogue: 50,0:12:27.70,0:12:30.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,that the people of the\NNorth Blue know very well.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:30.66,0:12:32.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's called "Noland, the Liar."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.79,0:12:33.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.87,0:12:36.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Stop looking at me, Luffy.\NMy name's not Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:36.52,0:12:37.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Is he right?
Dialogue: 50,0:12:37.69,0:12:40.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And is this island the one\Nmentioned in the fairy tale?
Dialogue: 50,0:12:40.61,0:12:43.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hmph. Yeah,\NNoland's my grandfather's,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.28,0:12:46.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,grandfather's grandfather. He's\Na distant ancestor of mine.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:47.03,0:12:48.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I am his descendant.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:48.95,0:12:50.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But we're so far removed,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.17,0:12:54.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I doubt there's even a single\Ndrop of his blood in my veins.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:54.20,0:12:55.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The Mont Blanc family\Nwas driven out
Dialogue: 50,0:12:55.79,0:12:57.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,of the North Blue country\Na long time ago,
Dialogue: 50,0:12:57.92,0:13:01.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and we've managed to keep\Na very low profile ever since.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:01.91,0:13:04.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,People still denounce\Nthe family name.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:04.04,0:13:05.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But we've never\Ndespised him for this.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:06.44,0:13:07.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NBut why?
Dialogue: 50,0:13:07.40,0:13:09.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Because Noland,\Ncontrary to popular belief,
Dialogue: 50,0:13:09.70,0:13:11.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,was an very honest person.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:11.37,0:13:13.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That's not what\Nthe fairy tale said.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.66,0:13:15.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NAs the story goes,
Dialogue: 50,0:13:15.24,0:13:18.37,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland's last words\Nwere as follows.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:18.40,0:13:21.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,"I can only assume that the\Ncity of gold sunk into the sea."
Dialogue: 50,0:13:21.86,0:13:22.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\t(2190,2774,\c&H818180&\3c&H818180&\4c&H818180&)}This line is accompanied
Dialogue: 50,0:13:22.78,0:13:25.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\t(2190,2774,\c&H818180&\3c&H818180&\4c&H818180&)}by an idiotic face\Nin the illustration.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:25.57,0:13:27.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\c&H818180&\3c&H818180&\4c&H818180&\t(1,600,\1c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&)}But Noland was no idiot.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:27.91,0:13:29.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\c&H818180&\3c&H818180&\4c&H818180&\t(1,600,\1c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&)}He knew what he saw,
Dialogue: 50,0:13:29.13,0:13:31.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\c&H818180&\3c&H818180&\4c&H818180&\t(1,600,\1c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&)}and I believe he\Nwasn't lying about it.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:31.30,0:13:33.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland was sure the\Nisland he stumbled upon,
Dialogue: 50,0:13:33.34,0:13:35.42,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,where he found\Nthe ruins of a city of gold,
Dialogue: 50,0:13:35.43,0:13:37.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,was the island of Jaya.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:37.35,0:13:40.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But when he returned with\Nthe king, there was no gold.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:40.93,0:13:43.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Unsuccessful, he insisted\Nthat the ancient city
Dialogue: 50,0:13:43.29,0:13:46.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,had submerged due\Nto shifts in the earth's crust.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:46.14,0:13:47.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But everyone dismissed this
Dialogue: 50,0:13:47.44,0:13:50.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,as the last‐ditch excuse\Nof a doomed man.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:50.69,0:13:53.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland was given\Na public execution.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:53.24,0:13:55.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,When he died,\Nso did his discoveries.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:55.58,0:13:57.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Only the legend\Nof the liar remained.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:57.55,0:13:58.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:58.56,0:13:59.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're trying to find\Nthe ancient city of gold
Dialogue: 50,0:13:59.64,0:14:00.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,at the bottom of the sea\Nin order to finally clear
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.73,0:14:03.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,the Mont Blanc family name\Nand prove Noland right.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:03.70,0:14:04.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.64,0:14:07.19,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NUsopp!
Dialogue: 50,0:14:09.48,0:14:11.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NI don't really\Ncare if the ancient city of gold
Dialogue: 50,0:14:11.29,0:14:12.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,exists or not.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:12.33,0:14:13.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The actions of my ancestor
Dialogue: 50,0:14:13.54,0:14:15.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,have nothing to do\Nwith me and my life.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:15.84,0:14:18.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You can't possibly begin to\Nimagine what it's like as a kid
Dialogue: 50,0:14:18.71,0:14:20.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,for everyone to laugh\Nat you and ridicule you
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.68,0:14:23.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,because you're a descendant\Nof that idiot, Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:23.22,0:14:25.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That's what I've dealt\Nwith my whole life.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:27.89,0:14:30.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NAnyway, over the past 400 years
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.47,0:14:31.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,a great many of my family
Dialogue: 50,0:14:31.74,0:14:35.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,have set sail to find the city\Nof gold, prove Noland right,
Dialogue: 50,0:14:35.74,0:14:38.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and restore the Mont Blanc name.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:38.44,0:14:40.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But each and every one\Nof them went missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.71,0:14:43.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I was ashamed to be a member\Nof such a pathetic family.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:43.75,0:14:46.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So I decided to leave\Nhome become a pirate.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:46.75,0:14:49.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wow! So you're\Na pirate just like us?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:49.35,0:14:51.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I didn't even really\Nwant to become a pirate.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:51.68,0:14:53.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I just wanted out\Nof Noland's shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.76,0:14:55.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,To be my own man.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:55.64,0:14:59.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But over time I came\Nto assemble my own pirate crew.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:59.18,0:15:02.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Finally, I was seen as a\Nleader, not a laughingstock.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:02.39,0:15:05.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And I spanned the world\Nlooking for adventures.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:05.44,0:15:09.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Then ten years ago as\Nmy crew and I sailed a calm sea,
Dialogue: 50,0:15:09.17,0:15:12.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,we discovered this island\Npurely by chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.01,0:15:13.05,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And ironically,
Dialogue: 50,0:15:13.10,0:15:15.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,of all my family members\Nwho sought out this place,
Dialogue: 50,0:15:15.69,0:15:19.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who lost their lives doing so,\Nit was I who found it.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:19.49,0:15:22.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I who despised\Nthe Mont Blanc name.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:22.44,0:15:26.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We came ashore, but found\Nno trace of the city of gold.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:26.19,0:15:27.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I stood on a cape of the island
Dialogue: 50,0:15:27.52,0:15:30.11,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and felt I was\Ndestined to be there.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:30.11,0:15:31.94,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Let's settle this, Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:31.98,0:15:33.66,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Once and for all.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:33.99,0:15:34.82,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,[UNDERLING A]\NYou're on your own.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:34.86,0:15:36.45,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,We don't want anything\Nto do with this.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:36.49,0:15:38.12,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,We're setting sail and leaving.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:38.12,0:15:39.37,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,[UNDERLING B]\NIf you wanna stay here
Dialogue: 50,0:15:39.41,0:15:43.54,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,and search for gold that doesn't\Nexist, you're doing it alone.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:43.58,0:15:45.82,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,[UNDERLING A]\NSo long, Captain.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:50.76,0:15:53.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NI don't care\Nif I find the city or not.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:53.39,0:15:56.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm not here to prove\NNoland right or wrong.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:56.10,0:15:58.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I have no interest\Nin rewriting history.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:59.23,0:16:02.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All I'm doing is following\Nwhat I believe is my destiny.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:02.57,0:16:06.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This is between me and Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:06.24,0:16:07.82,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm facing what I fear,
Dialogue: 50,0:16:07.87,0:16:12.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and whatever the outcome,\Nthe act is all that matters.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:14.14,0:16:16.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wow. What a sad story.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:17.86,0:16:19.02,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But what about the monkeys.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:19.05,0:16:22.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,How did they come to be on\Nthis island with you anyways?
Dialogue: 50,0:16:22.47,0:16:24.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[USOPP]\NI'm sure that's\Nanother story of bravery
Dialogue: 50,0:16:24.76,0:16:26.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and the face of incredible odds.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:26.47,0:16:29.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Your life reads like a great\Nbook you know, Cricket?
Dialogue: 50,0:16:29.25,0:16:31.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They were just\Nfans of the fairy tale.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:31.29,0:16:32.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They're fans?
Dialogue: 50,0:16:32.69,0:16:34.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NHow did they find you?
Dialogue: 50,0:16:34.67,0:16:36.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I think it was\Nfive or six years ago.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:36.76,0:16:39.51,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They heard a rumor\Nand set out to find me.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:39.58,0:16:42.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Those two truly believe that the\Ncity of gold exists somewhere.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:42.92,0:16:44.96,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And they're helping me find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.00,0:16:47.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Ahhh!
Dialogue: 50,0:16:47.27,0:16:50.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Shojo, you have no idea\Nwhat you just got yourself into!
Dialogue: 50,0:16:50.48,0:16:51.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Bring it on you big ape.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:51.63,0:16:52.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm ready when you are.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:52.76,0:16:54.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Just step up and\Nyou'll get knocked down.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:54.76,0:16:57.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NThe sea surrounding\Nthis island is very deep.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:57.72,0:16:59.60,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And in those dark, cold depths,
Dialogue: 50,0:16:59.64,0:17:02.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,you're surrounded by a\Nprofound sense of solitude.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:04.44,0:17:05.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NWhen I first arrived here,
Dialogue: 50,0:17:05.69,0:17:09.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I spent my time searching\Nthe sea bed alone.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:09.41,0:17:10.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They entered my life\Nwithout permission
Dialogue: 50,0:17:10.99,0:17:14.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and assigned themselves\Nas my crew without asking.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:14.38,0:17:16.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And they do nothing\Nbut fight all the time.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:16.83,0:17:19.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But having these idiots\Naround puts me at ease.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:19.88,0:17:22.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And truthfully,\NI enjoy their company.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:23.63,0:17:24.82,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You understand?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:25.21,0:17:27.34,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I understand completely.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:27.38,0:17:28.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,True friends lift each other up
Dialogue: 50,0:17:28.79,0:17:31.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and give each other\Nstrength in times of need.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:31.48,0:17:34.23,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Are you just about finished\Ntelling us your life story?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:34.27,0:17:35.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Shut your mouth\Nyou ungrateful brat.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.89,0:17:38.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[screams]
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.53,0:17:39.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Stop it.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:39.63,0:17:43.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Look, all I really want to\Nknow about is sky island.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.22,0:17:44.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET chuckles]
Dialogue: 50,0:17:44.43,0:17:46.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're a pushy guy, aren't ya?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:46.47,0:17:48.14,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But like I told you earlier,
Dialogue: 50,0:17:48.21,0:17:51.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,the only person who's ever\Nseen the sky island is Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:51.26,0:17:53.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And nobody knows\Nif he was telling the truth
Dialogue: 50,0:17:53.26,0:17:55.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,or if it was just\Nanother tall tale.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:55.48,0:17:57.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[LUFFY]\NIs there any record\Nof his trip to the island?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:57.81,0:18:01.19,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Officially, no, but he\Ndoes mention it in here.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:01.27,0:18:02.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What do you have there?
Dialogue: 50,0:18:02.40,0:18:04.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That isn't\NNoland's logbook, is it?
Dialogue: 50,0:18:04.62,0:18:05.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NYeah, it is.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:05.91,0:18:08.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Read from the\Nbottom of that page.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:08.66,0:18:09.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NAmazing.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:09.73,0:18:12.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This logbook is\Nover 400 years old.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:12.61,0:18:14.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,June 21st, year 1120.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:14.90,0:18:16.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A sunny day on the\NSea of Ephemeris.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:16.91,0:18:19.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Upon departing\Nfrom the Jolly Villa.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:19.30,0:18:21.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We left the harbor and\Nsailed into the rising sun
Dialogue: 50,0:18:21.64,0:18:23.55,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,at a heading of\Neast by northeast
Dialogue: 50,0:18:23.60,0:18:25.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,with the wind at out back.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.86,0:18:29.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,At midday we happened across\Na bumboat carrying a rare item.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:29.95,0:18:33.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A single person contraption\Ncalled a sky waver.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:33.46,0:18:36.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This small, mysterious vessel\Ncan generate its own wind
Dialogue: 50,0:18:36.50,0:18:39.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and sail at great speeds\Neven on a still day.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:39.12,0:18:41.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But the ski‐like ship\Nwas not easily maneuvered.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:41.63,0:18:42.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I couldn't control it,
Dialogue: 50,0:18:42.74,0:18:45.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,although my crew has\Ntaken quite a liking to it.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:45.20,0:18:46.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I gotta get one of those things.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.92,0:18:49.01,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Keep going!\NDon't stop reading!
Dialogue: 50,0:18:49.05,0:18:51.55,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NUh, we were told the\Nvessel had been manufactured
Dialogue: 50,0:18:51.59,0:18:52.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,on the sky island,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.84,0:18:55.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and that many more interesting\Ndevices could be found there.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:55.81,0:18:57.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It brought to mind\Nan explorer friend of mine
Dialogue: 50,0:18:57.68,0:18:59.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who once showed me\Nthe most unusual specimen,
Dialogue: 50,0:18:59.81,0:19:01.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,a living sky fish.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:01.66,0:19:03.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I have never seen a fish with\Nsuch a bizarre appearance
Dialogue: 50,0:19:03.91,0:19:05.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\an1\q2\pos(721.5,1053)}– in all my years.\N– Sky fish?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:05.74,0:19:08.37,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[NAMI]\NThis island remains\Nthe only unexplored domain,
Dialogue: 50,0:19:08.41,0:19:10.92,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and as a sailor and adventurer\NI feel it is my destiny
Dialogue: 50,0:19:10.96,0:19:13.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to one day reach\Nthe sea in the sky.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:13.13,0:19:14.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Mont Blanc Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:14.72,0:19:16.01,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you know what this means?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:16.01,0:19:17.93,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The sky island\Nmust really exist.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:17.97,0:19:19.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Just like Robin said it did!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:19.85,0:19:22.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Now we just gotta\Nfigure out how to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.31,0:19:24.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CHOPPER]\NThe sky island does exist!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:27.56,0:19:28.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[MASIRA]\NYou're up?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:28.48,0:19:29.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You feeling all right?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:29.76,0:19:30.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Better than ever.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:30.70,0:19:31.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Glad to hear it.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:31.91,0:19:34.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[MASIRA]\NThis jerk snuck up\Non me and attacked me from...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.65,0:19:35.35,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,[CRICKET]\NShut up.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:35.35,0:19:36.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I need to ask you something.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:36.81,0:19:38.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What do you think of those guys?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:38.18,0:19:40.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why you askin', Old‐timer?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:40.15,0:19:41.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It seems that they're\Ndetermined to get
Dialogue: 50,0:19:41.94,0:19:44.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to sky island no matter what.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:44.55,0:19:46.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Sky island?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:46.08,0:19:48.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You know there's only\None way for them to get there.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:48.80,0:19:51.14,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And if they try\Nto get there on their own,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.18,0:19:52.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,they'll die.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:52.72,0:19:54.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:54.22,0:19:56.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I think we should\Nhelp them along.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:56.47,0:19:58.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So, what do you\Nguys think about that?
Comment: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{=51}===============================DIALOGUE============================
